  "caveats": [
    "WorldPop's modelling uses built-settlement layers as covariates (a covariate relationship with footprints is likely but its form is not recorded for this raster); if the product is building-constrained, V1 tests the consistency of the footprint layer with the surface, not the accuracy of population counts.",
    "OSM building mapping is volunteered and uneven; Microsoft footprints are machine-detected and uncorrected. See completeness table.",
    "The threshold (rho > 0.60) was declared on the OSM layer, which fails at the 1 km grid scale; the Microsoft layer was added afterwards. See sequence."
